results/data_v2/README.md:6:# AndroidAgent-SFT-v2
research_notes/Beating GUI Owl at 2B fairly/training_tunables.md:113:There is still no AW-measured LoRA-vs-full or frozen-vs-unfrozen-vision ablation at ≤4B. Nearly every 2026 small-agent paper uses **full-parameter training with the vision encoder unfrozen**: GUI-Libra (lr 1e-5), UI-Oceanus (2–4B SFT lr 1e-5), GUI-SD-v2 and VeriGUI. The most useful new curves are (a) Ferret-UI Lite-3B, where adding diverse synthetic *online-collected* trajectories kept raising AW (19.6→25.2 at 17K), and (b) evidence that narrow SFT causes forgetting at 2B while OPD and RL do not. Epoch guidance conflicts across papers.
research_notes/Beating GUI Owl at 2B fairly/training_tunables.md:143:- Our setup (LoRA r64, about 0.4–0.5 epoch, vision frozen) differs from every recent small-agent recipe on two axes: adapter vs full, and vision frozen vs trained. No GUI paper isolates either axis on AW, so the lever is untested, not disproven. The VLA evidence and LFM2-VL's own 5:5:1 joint training suggest a cheap probe: LoRA on the vision encoder as well, or unfreezing the projector. A projector-only unfreeze costs little memory on a 96GB card.
research_notes/Small GUI agent training methods/architecture_hparams.md:212:- **Vision tower (adjacent evidence, not GUI):** in a π0 VLA LoRA study, performance saturated at r=32. "Freezing the VLM or restricting the vision encoder to LoRA significantly degrades performance"; full vision-encoder fine-tuning plus LoRA r=32 matched full fine-tuning. — [arXiv 2607.10172](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.10172). Contrast: on general multimodal benchmarks, existing visual fine-tuning methods "fail to consistently outperform the frozen baseline". — [CoVFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.21077)
research_notes/Small GUI agent training methods/architecture_hparams.md:223:- No GUI-agent paper found compares LoRA vs full fine-tuning, or frozen vs tuned vision tower, at <=3B on AW.
["--src", "experimentalmachines/AndroidAgent-SFT-v2", "--rev", "42f7f763649d4d2c73eeb99ff5f0bc33bd15a16a", "--labels_repo", "alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-SFT-v3", "--out_repo", "alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-SFT-v3", "--work", "/content/data/v3build"]["--src", "experimentalmachines/AndroidAgent-SFT-v2", "--rev", "42f7f763649d4d2c73eeb99ff5f0bc33bd15a16a", "--out_repo", "alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-SFT-v3", "--teacher", "Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct", "--bs", "32"]"""v3 data = v2 data with every blank training intent filled (runs ON a Colab GPU).

Why: LFM3-VL-2B trained on v2 emitted an empty <think> on 52% of AndroidWorld steps (v1: 0%) because 8,739 v2 rows
(AMEX: no per-step instruction; GUI-Odyssey: model-generated instructions blanked when they contradicted the action)
carry an empty intent. Small agents trained without intents act blindly (MIRAGE: action-only SFT < base).

Fill rule (the action itself is never changed):
  click / long_press -> a teacher VLM (Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct) sees the training screenshot with a red ring at the
                        recorded point plus the goal, and writes ONE short AndroidControl-style instruction
                        ("Click on the search bar."). Unusable outputs -> the row is dropped (counted).
  scroll / input_text / navigate_* / keyboard_enter / wait / open_app -> deterministic AC-style templates.
History lines are left as they are. Dev splits are copied unchanged (their intents are not scored).

usage: python vm_v3_intents.py --src experimentalmachines/AndroidAgent-SFT-v2 --rev <sha> \
         --out_repo alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-SFT-v3 [--teacher Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct --bs 32]
"""
import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import time
from collections import Counter

import torch
from datasets import DatasetDict, load_dataset
from huggingface_hub import HfApi
from PIL import ImageDraw
from transformers import AutoModelForImageTextToText, AutoProcessor

p = argparse.ArgumentParser()
p.add_argument("--src", required=True)
p.add_argument("--rev", required=True)
p.add_argument("--out_repo", required=True)
p.add_argument("--teacher", default="Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct")
p.add_argument("--bs", type=int, default=32)
p.add_argument("--limit", type=int, default=0, help="debug: label at most N teacher rows")
p.add_argument("--labels_from", default="", help="rebuild from saved labels (stats/v3_intent_labels.json in this "
               "dataset repo) instead of running the teacher; CPU only")
